+## Objective
+Rounds 1 to 4 tried to read nested shell constructs (substitutions, here-documents, backtick bodies, subshells) and each lost refusals in the interactions between them. A second resolution round decided a smaller design (`docs/CHANGES.md`, the entry "2026-11-15 TASK-063: second resolution round", read it whole; its material is `handoff/RESOLUTION-TASK-063-2.md`): **the guard reads one flat grammar, in which every command is one list of complete words, and refuses every other command as unreadable**, its reason holding `cannot read` and naming the form, so the agent rewrites it. This round **deletes the reader of rounds 3 and 4 and writes the flat reader in its place**: one loop over the characters, holding nothing but the current quote state, the current word and the current command. Every check the guard already makes then reads complete word lists. Build exactly the grammar below and nothing beyond it; where this brief is silent, the CHANGES entry is the authority.
