+Round 4's code (this brief's commit) is your starting tree. Keep the checks that read words where they are right: `snapshot_subject`, `around_the_shim`, `program_behind`, `git_subcommand`, `force_push_reason`, `merge_reason`, `premerge_recorded`, `hook_skipper_option`, `in_worktree`, `gh_words` (with requirement 7's change), the alias, hooks-path, graphql, merge-endpoint and launcher-bypass checks in `_check_one`. Delete `read_shell`, `_ansi_c_decode`, `_strip_outer_parens`, `_parsed_snapshot`, `_heredoc_shell_reads`, `_heredoc_body`, `iter_commands`, and every helper that only they use; rewrite `split_commands`, `chain_parts`, `words`, `chain_reason`, `commit_message`, `leading_husky_zero`, `strip_prefix`, `shell_inner` and `_check_one` on the new reading. Other tests call these names, which stay with these signatures: `check(command, cwd=None, tool="Bash")`, `words(text)`, `state_changing(w)`, `STATE_GIT` (`tests/test_allowlist.py`), `merge_reason(args, cwd)` (`tests/test_release_s_records_gate.py`), `premerge_recorded(sha, cwd)` (monkeypatched by `tests/test_allowlist.py`).
